Version 0.3.1 -- 2026-08-11

    This version improves performance on x86 platforms.

  Improvements

    * SSE2 kernel has been massively improved; it is now roughly 5 times faster
      than the scalar implementation. For an Ocarina of Time 1.0 US ROM, this
      brings compression times down from 16 to about 3.2 seconds.


Version 0.3 -- 2026-08-11

    This version adds major optimizations for libyaz0 on x86 platforms.

  Features

    * Dynamic dispatch for compress search function.
    * New functions to query the search algorithm.
    * Search algorithm selection when initializing a compression stream.

  Improvements

    * This release adds a SSE2 kernel for the compressor's longest substring
      search and match length algorithms. This massively speeds up compression
      on x86 hosts. The gains are around 2.5x on the compression of a full
      Nintendo 64 Zelda ROM.


Version 0.2.0 -- 2026-08-09

    This version adds several utility functions.

  Features

    * The compression can now be initialized with values for alignment hint and
      the reserved bytes in the Yaz0 header.
    * Runtime version query functions.

  Improvements

    * Added a reset function for the compressor and decompressor.
    * Added a function to get human readable descriptions of result codes.
    * Added a utility function to calculate upper bound compressed size.


Version 0.1.1 -- 2026-08-09

    Documentation improvements and minor bugs.

  Improvements

    * Added a configuration header with version macros.
    * The public header is now documented.
    * Removed an implicit conversion.


Version 0.1.0 -- 2026-07-31

    First public release.

  Features

    * Streaming compression and decompression of the Yaz0 format.
    * Compression levels 0 through 9, plus YAZ0_DEFAULT_COMPRESSION.
      Level 0 stores the input without searching for matches.
    * Support for custom memory allocators
    * Utilities for reading and writing Yaz0 headers

  Correctness

    * Output is byte-exact with Nintendo's Nintendo 64 encoder.
    * Compressor and decompressor have been tested against every file in
      the 1.0 (US) releases of Ocarina of Time and Majora's Mask.
    * Special care was taken to reject malformed input.
    * Test suite with synthetic tests to check against edge cases.

  Compatibility

    * No API or ABI stability is guaranteed before version 1.0.

  Known limitations

    * The vectorized code paths described in the README are not
      implemented yet.
    * yaz0_compress_init does not expose the alignment hint or the
      reserved bytes of the Yaz0 header, and writes zeros for both.
